  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The ongoing investigation into Master Bank and its associated entities continues to generate scrutiny regarding the Federal Police's reporting processes. Reports submitted by the Federal Police to the Supreme Court have undergone modifications, with the agency stating these changes strictly follow orders issued by Justice Fachin. This has led to the exclusion of certain references involving public figures, sparking debate among legal observers and investigators about the transparency and potential limitations of the current findings. Federal Police leadership maintains that the Prosecutor General's Office and the Supreme Court already hold the complete evidentiary material extracted from mobile devices related to Daniel Vorcaro. Meanwhile, the legal proceedings also encompass separate requests from the BRB regarding resources, with Justice Fachin ordering relevant parties to submit formal statements regarding the bank's liquidation status.",
